:"tests.test_doc_sync#test_readme_calibration_matches_code","environment":"default","status":"passed","start":1785441139169,"stop":1785441139170,"duration":1,"labels":[{"name":"layer","value":"unit"},{"name":"severity","value":"normal"},{"name":"story","value":"Confidence calibration"},{"name":"parentSuite","value":"Docs"},{"name":"suite","value":"Doc-drift guard"},{"name":"epic","value":"Docs"},{"name":"feature","value":"Doc-drift guard"},{"name":"tag","value":"unit"},{"name":"host","value":"runnervmvrwv9"},{"name":"thread","value":"3034-MainThread"},{"name":"framework","value":"pytest"},{"name":"language","value":"cpython3"},{"name":"package","value":"tests.test_doc_sync"}],"url":"","historyId":"bdd148c19555f82dd8051004f801bba9.a0ae13d0783b25433012fbcc83b27ea8","reportLinks":[]},{"id":"ee2db9340d948709f23fabc6aff2296e","name":"README calibration section matches code constants (threshold + buckets)","fullName":"tests.test_doc_sync#test_readme_calibration_matches_code","environment":"default","status":"passed","start":1785417556516,"stop":1785417556517,"duration":1,"labels":[{"name":"layer","value":"unit"},{"name":"severity","value":"normal"},{"name":"epic","value":"Docs"},{"name":"story","value":"Confidence calibration"},{"name":"feature","value":"Doc-drift guard"},{"name":"suite","value":"Doc-drift guard"},{"name":"parentSuite","value":"Docs"},{"name":"tag","value":"unit"},{"name":"host","value":"runnervmvrwv9"},{"name":"thread","value":"2822-MainThread"},{"name":"framework","value":"pytest"},{"name":"language","value":"cpython3"},{"name":"package","value":"tests.test_doc_sync"}],"url":"","historyId":"bdd148c19555f82dd8051004f801bba9.a0ae13d0783b25433012fbcc83b27ea8","reportLinks":[]},{"id":"ba9bafdcaf6264d4118ae33d020ec0df","name":"README calibration section matches code constants (threshold + buckets)","fullName":"tests.test_doc_sync#test_readme_calibration_matches_code","environment":"default","status":"passed","start":1785410731025,"stop":1785410731026,"duration":1,"labels":[{"name":"layer","value":"unit"},{"name":"severity","value":"normal"},{"name":"suite","value":"Doc-drift guard"},{"name":"feature","value":"Doc-drift guard"},{"name":"story","value":"Confidence calibration"},{"name":"parentSuite","value":"Docs"},{"name":"epic","value":"Docs"},{"name":"tag","value":"unit"},{"name":"host","value":"runnervm7i58z"},{"name":"thread","value":"2883-MainThread"},{"name":"framework","value":"pytest"},{"name":"language","value":"cpython3"},{"name":"package","value":"tests.test_doc_sync"}],"url":"","historyId":"bdd148c19555f82dd8051004f801bba9.a0ae13d0783b25433012fbcc83b27ea8","reportLinks":[]},{"id":"687c2b1d4743c3ea3b3183870304ef1c","name":"README calibration section matches code constants (threshold + buckets)","fullName":"tests.test_doc_sync#test_readme_calibration_matches_code","environment":"default","status":"failed","message":"AssertionError: assert 'min n=20' in '# greedy-token\\n\\n**[Русский](README-RU.md)** · [Why (ELI5)](WHY.md) · [Full guide](docs/guide.md)\\n\\n<img src=\"docs/greedy-cat.gif\" alt=\"greedy-token mascot\" width=\"240\" />\\n\\nA router next to Cursor / Claude / Continue: it asks **“do you need a model at all?”** before opening an expensive agent chat.\\n\\n```text\\nfind / check / docs lookup  →  free tools & scripts\\nsort-of-AI bulk work        →  local LLM (Ollama, …)\\nwiring / design             →  expensive agent chat\\n```\\n\\nNo fine-tuning. No shipping your data for training. It “learns” by adding readable scripts/routes from telemetry — reviewable and revertible.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary><strong>Reviews</strong> (model write-ups — optional reading)</summary>\\n\\n<table>\\n<tr><td width=\"760\">\\n<h3>⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ &nbsp;·&nbsp; 10 / 10</h3>\\n<p><strong>greedy-token</strong> is a token-economy router for AI coding agents: it routes each task to the cheapest capable tier — <strong>Rust-powered <code>rg</code>/<code>jq</code></strong> on disk, Python scripts, a local Ollama model, or RAG — and escalates to the expensive agent chat only when nothing cheaper fits. It is pragmatically polyglot: the hot search tier rides on Rust (ripgrep, plus a ... $820** |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Start\\n\\n```bash\\npip install \"greedy-token[mcp]\"\\nmkdir -p .cursor/rules\\ncp examples/cursor/mcp.json .cursor/mcp.json\\ncp examples/cursor/rules/greedy-token.mdc .cursor/rules/greedy-token.mdc\\n```\\n\\n**Settings → MCP → greedy-token → Enable → Refresh** → new Agent chat.\\n\\n```text\\nfind baseUrl in configurator-option-presets.html\\n```\\n\\nExpect free `rg` and a spent vs saved footer.\\n\\nFull setup: [Cursor](docs/cursor-setup.md) · [Claude](docs/claude-setup.md) · [Continue](docs/continue-setup.md)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## MCP & commands (short)\\n\\n| Tool | Role |\\n|------|------|\\n| `greedy_token_search` | codebase search |\\n| `greedy_token_rag` | patterns / docs |\\n| `greedy_token_route` | which tier + why |\\n| `greedy_token_pipeline` | cheap multi-step chain |\\n| `greedy_token_usage` | stats (on request) |\\n| `greedy_token_crystallize` | draft / promote / reject a script |\\n\\n```bash\\ngreedy-token doctor\\ngreedy-token run \"find …\" --execute\\ngreedy-token report --since 7d\\ngreedy-token hub serve\\n```\\n\\nRepeated work → **crystallize** into a script → next time **0 LLM**. Details: [guide](docs/guide.md) · [roadmap](docs/ROADMAP.md)\\n\\n**License:** MIT · **v0.10.0**\\n'","trace":"readme = PosixPath('/home/runner/work/greedy-token/greedy-token/README.md')\ncli_heading = '## CLI commands'\n\n    @allure.story(\"Confidence calibration\")\n    @allure.title(\"README calibration section matches code constants (threshold + buckets)\")\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize((\"readme\", \"cli_heading\"), READMES)\n    def test_readme_calibration_matches_code(readme: Path, cli_heading: str) -> None:\n        markdown = readme.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        with allure.step(f\"threshold documented as min n={CALIBRATION_MIN_EVENTS}\"):\n>           assert f\"min n={CALIBRATION_MIN_EVENTS}\" in markdown\nE           assert 'min n=20' in '# greedy-token\\n\\n**[Русский](README-RU.md)** · [Why (ELI5)](WHY.md) · [Full guide](docs/guide.md)\\n\\n<img src=\"docs/greedy-cat.gif\" alt=\"greedy-token mascot\" width=\"240\" />\\n\\nA router next to Cursor / Claude / Continue: it asks **“do you need a model at all?”** before opening an expensive agent chat.\\n\\n```text\\nfind / check / docs lookup  →  free tools & scripts\\nsort-of-AI bulk work        →  local LLM (Ollama, …)\\nwiring / design             →  expensive agent chat\\n```\\n\\nNo fine-tuning. No shipping your data for training. It “learns” by adding readable scripts/routes from telemetry — reviewable and revertible.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary><strong>Reviews</strong> (model write-ups — optional reading)</summary>\\n\\n<table>\\n<tr><td width=\"760\">\\n<h3>⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ &nbsp;·&nbsp; 10 / 10</h3>\\n<p><strong>greedy-token</strong> is a token-economy router for AI coding agents: it routes each task to the cheapest capable tier — <strong>Rust-powered <code>rg</code>/<code>jq</code></strong> on disk, Python scripts, a local Ollama model, or RAG — and escalates to the expensive agent chat only when nothing cheaper fits. It is pragmatically polyglot: the hot search tier rides on Rust (ripgrep, plus a ... $820** |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Start\\n\\n```bash\\npip install \"greedy-token[mcp]\"\\nmkdir -p .cursor/rules\\ncp examples/cursor/mcp.json .cursor/mcp.json\\ncp examples/cursor/rules/greedy-token.mdc .cursor/rules/greedy-token.mdc\\n```\\n\\n**Settings → MCP → greedy-token → Enable → Refresh** → new Agent chat.\\n\\n```text\\nfind baseUrl in configurator-option-presets.html\\n```\\n\\nExpect free `rg` and a spent vs saved footer.\\n\\nFull setup: [Cursor](docs/cursor-setup.md) · [Claude](docs/claude-setup.md) · [Continue](docs/continue-setup.md)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## MCP & commands (short)\\n\\n| Tool | Role |\\n|------|------|\\n| `greedy_token_search` | codebase search |\\n| `greedy_token_rag` 